    {
      "id": "1286510312299958294",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2024-09-20T02:12:40.658+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Yodle is a name that many people outside of TRTHNBB and its diplomatic partners will likely not be familiar with. However, over the development of this proposal, Yodle’s exemplary deeds are given the worldwide spotlight they truly deserve. This proposal is a brilliant example of uplifting a diamond in the rough and demonstrating the hard work that goes into founding and maintaining a UCR with the cultural strength and political excellence of TRTHNBB, which has arisen as one of TEP’s most active and closest partner regions in recent days.\n\nThe proposal itself is well-written from the perspective of a region-mate familiar with Yodle’s work. Their resilience is highlighted immediately and developed over the course of the resolution. Their commitment to regionbuilding, including the Social Reformer, one of the most high quality regional newspapers in the game, a highly successful endotarting initiative, and their legislative legwork shines bright and true. It is not easy to create a successful region and there is no formula for it, but Yodle has risen to the challenge and met it.\n\nTheir flexibility and depth is showcased as well — not only is Yodle a titan on their own, but has been known to mentor and uplift the great leaders of their region as any good founder should, who form the core of the political population to this date and are all crucial as well to TRTHNBB’s recent diplomatic revolution. On top of it all, as a card collector, Yodle has distinguished themselves in yet another way worthy of praise, with many unique collections to their name.\n\nThe author has shown a great propensity to incorporate feedback and was keen from the start to hear from The East Pacific. For their hard work and that of Yodle, and for the great relationship we have developed with a region that would not exist, and certainly not in its current form, without the strong guidance of a figure such as them, The East Pacific is happy to vote FOR this resolution.",
      "author": {
        "id": "738186404399415336",
        "name": "theconstantofchange",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Mango",
        "color": null,
